--- a/specs/state.md
+++ b/specs/state.md
@@ -592,6 +592,28 @@
 - Resume boundary
   - Because call frames add new durable lineage and resume keys, resume from pre-`schema_version: "2.1"` state is rejected unless a tested upgrader ships with the same tranche.
 
+## Derived Pure-Result Persistence Profile (`derived_pure_replay.v1`)
+
+State schema stays `2.1`; the profile is an additive, optional root/frame field.
+
+- Selector
+  - `RunState.result_persistence_profile` is optional. Absent means the historical bundle-backed persistence and `to_dict()` omits the key; `from_dict()` of a payload without it yields `None`.
+  - The only supported value is `derived_pure_replay.v1`. Any other present value fails closed with `ValueError` at `RunState` construction, `StateManager.initialize(...)`, and on load; a failed load leaves the state file byte-for-byte unchanged.
+  - `StateManager.initialize(..., result_persistence_profile=None)` writes the field atomically with the new run state, before any visit. Ordinary loads never infer, backfill or upgrade it.
+  - Automatic selection: a compiled typed public `.orc` `orchestrator run`, a new root created by `orchestrator resume --force-restart`, and a fresh non-iterative call frame whose callee bundle has `provenance.frontend_kind == "workflow_lisp"` (including a fresh retry after a failed predecessor, which stays unchanged). Existing roots/frames, non-Workflow-Lisp callees and iteration-owned frames keep the historical profile; an existing frame is never backfilled, and one without a mapping `state` is rejected with `ValueError` ("existing call-frame state") before any write.
+- Eligibility
+  - A compiler-generated `pure_projection` is replay-eligible when it is acyclic and visited at most once per scope. Recurrent, loop-owned and other multiply visited nodes (and pure nodes reading them) keep full rows, bundles and checkpoints, recorded in `ineligible_pure_reasons` (for example `multiple_visit_region`).
+  - `derive_pure_result_replay_index(bundle)` derives the dependency index without changing the serialized runtime plan. Refs are scoped to the bundle that holds them.
+- Value-free completion shell
+  - A successful eligible visit persists exactly `{"name", "step_id", "visit_count": 1, "status": "completed", "exit_code": 0, "outcome": {"status": "completed", "phase": "execution", "class": "completed", "retryable": false}, "result_storage": "derived_pure_replay.v1"}`; no value, artifact, debug or timing key. Failed and skipped rows stay full rows.
+  - Visit begin (visit increment + running cursor) and settlement (shell or full failure row + cursor clear) are each one atomic state transaction. Interrupted visits are reused without a second increment.
+  - `classify_pure_replay_progress` yields `unstarted`, `interrupted`, `derived_complete`, `durable_failure_skip`, or `progress_witness_invalid` for any other visit/cursor/row combination (including any visit two).
+- Resume
+  - Before the prologue, resume audits that no eligible node has a persisted value row, pure bundle, private-lineage entry, checkpoint record or restore binding (`profile_conflict`, `context.surface` in `steps`, `pure_bundle`, `private_artifact_versions`, `checkpoint_record`, `restore_payload`) and that progress witnesses are valid.
+  - Completed eligible values are then re-derived in memory from validated durable leaves (bound inputs and durable results). Replay never dispatches an effect, increments a visit, settles a result or writes durable state. Failure is the terminal error `pure_result_replay_unavailable` with `context.reason` one of `durable_input_missing`, `durable_input_invalid`, `binding_unresolved`, `evaluation_failed`, `output_contract_invalid`, `progress_witness_invalid`, `profile_conflict`, `dependency_index_invalid`, `reachability_ambiguous`, `multiple_visit_region`.
+  - The restart boundary is determined once per resume and passed to the default-resume decision.
+  - Eligible pure points emit no checkpoint record and are excluded from durable restore candidates before unique-nearest selection; the restart node keeps node-local authority. The one zero-record default-resume case is `restore_decision` `VALIDATED_FRAME_ENTRY_REPLAY` (`selection_reason` `validated_frame_entry_replay`, null `checkpoint_id`), requiring validated bound-input leaves and exact profile/progress witnesses; otherwise it fails closed with `lexical_default_resume_prior_boundary_not_restorable`.
+
 ## State File Schema (example)
 
 The state file (`${RUN_ROOT}/state.json`) is the authoritative record of execution:
